---
import { cardCls, crumbCls } from '../lib/ui';
// One lab (#/leaderboard/lab/<key>; /api/lab, thorp.labs): the maker of a family of outside models, its models, and
// its five best and five worst readings on the rungs of the four chains, each set against the other labs' models on
// the same test (its standing: lift less the field's median, over the field's spread). UI.md, "Leaderboard".
---
<div class="section" id="lab">
  <h1><a class={crumbCls('back')} href="/leaderboard">← leaderboard</a> <span id="labtitle"></span> <span class="q" id="labnav"></span></h1>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><div class="rungover" id="labover"></div></section>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
    <h2>Its best <span class="note">the five readings where its models most beat the other labs' models on the same test</span></h2>
    <div class="scroll"><table id="labbest" data-nosort><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
    <h2>Its worst <span class="note">the five readings where its models most trail the other labs' models on the same test</span></h2>
    <div class="scroll"><table id="labworst" data-nosort><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    <p class="note mt">Every rung of the four chains (the chain grades, s4.outside_readings), read for each of the lab's models. A reading's standing is its lift less the median of the other labs' models on that test, over their spread (σ, the standard deviation), so a test where every model lifts 2.0 does not crowd out one where the field lifts 0.1. "Beats" counts the other labs' models it lifts higher than. ✓ performed: lift 0.1 and two in three right.</p>
  </section>
</div>
